+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+Reproduction (`.bdk/runs/fix-total-crash/debug/reproduction.md`), way in tools.e2e cli: in an empty directory `tally add 5` prints `Added 5.00` and exits 0, then `tally total` exits 1 with `TypeError: total.toFixed is not a function` at bin/tally.js:20. Expected `Total: 5.00` per spec tally, Requirement: Total. See proposal.md for why.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+
+- `ledger.json` holds numbers, so `total` sums numbers.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+
+- Migrating or tolerating ledgers already written with text entries.
+
+## Decisions
+
+### D1. Root cause: `add` stores the text argument
+
+bin/tally.js:16 `entries.push(value)` pushes `value`, the raw argv string, though `parseAmount(value)` already returned the number `amount` at line 14. `ledger.json` holds `["5"]`. At bin/tally.js:19 `total` runs `reduce((sum, amount) => sum + amount, 0)`: `0 + "5"` is the string `"05"`, so `total` is a string and `total.toFixed` at line 20 throws. The empty ledger works because the initial `0` stays a number.
+
+### D2. Fix: push the parsed `amount`
+
+Change line 16 to `entries.push(amount)`. Alternatives: coerce in `total` (`Number(amount)`) loses to the fix at the source, since it leaves bad data on disk and hides the next reader's bug; coerce in `load()` likewise, and it would also mask invalid entries. Both could be added later to read old ledgers (out of scope).
+
+Call sites: `add` (line 14 to 18) is the only writer of `ledger.json`; `total` (line 19) is the only reader besides `add`'s own `load()`, and it gets numbers as it expects. `parseAmount` in src/parse.js is unchanged. The `Added` output already uses `amount`.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [A ledger.json written before the fix holds text entries and `total` still fails on it] -> out of scope; deleting the file or a later Change that reads old entries.
